# Trivy filesystem-scan suppressions. Mirrors the rationale in
# `deny.toml` so both audit signals stay in sync.
#
# hickory-proto / hickory-net DNS DoS bugs (NSEC3 unbounded loop, and
# the sibling O(n²) name-compression bug if Trivy ever picks it up).
# Both reachable through iroh's address-lookup path, which the node
# runtime exercises in normal operation via `presets::N0`. The DoS
# surface is bounded to DNS lookups (an attacker would need to inject
# crafted responses), but this is not a dead path.
#
# Fixed in hickory-proto 0.26.1, but iroh 0.98 exact-pins
# =0.26.0-beta.4 — drop this ignore once upstream iroh bumps. Tracked
# in `deny.toml` as RUSTSEC-2026-0119 / RUSTSEC-2026-0120.
#
# When iroh > 0.98 lands and brings hickory >= 0.26.1, remove this
# entry in the same PR that bumps the iroh dep, alongside the
# matching `deny.toml` ignores.
GHSA-3v94-mw7p-v465
